Bundled adversarial corpus — sources, licenses, attribution.

This skill vendors recognized, permissively-licensed academic safety benchmarks
for DEFENSIVE evaluation (testing whether an application refuses/handles
adversarial inputs). The prompts are attacker *requests* and benign controls —
not operational instructions. Use only against systems you are authorized to test.

PromptInject  (Perez & Ribeiro, 2022)  — MIT
  https://github.com/agencyenterprise/PromptInject
  injection (goal hijacking), data_leakage (prompt leaking), benign controls.
  Generated into JSONL by scripts/build_promptinject_corpus.py.

AdvBench  (Zou et al., "Universal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks")  — MIT
  https://github.com/llm-attacks/llm-attacks  (data/advbench/harmful_behaviors.csv)
  520 harmful behavior requests. Used as refusal targets (harmful_content).

CyberSecEval / PurpleLlama  (Meta)  — MIT
  https://github.com/meta-llama/PurpleLlama  (CybersecurityBenchmarks/datasets)
  - prompt_injection/prompt_injection.json  (251 textual prompt-injection cases;
    each case's native judge_question is reused as the per-test rubric).
  - mitre_frr/mitre_frr.json  (750 benign security tasks; false-refusal controls).

XSTest  (Röttger et al., 2023)  — CC-BY-4.0  (attribution required)
  https://github.com/paul-rottger/xstest  (xstest_prompts.csv)
  250 safe prompts (over-refusal controls) + 200 unsafe (harmful_content).

NOT bundled (opt-in runtime fetch via scripts/build_corpus.py flags):
  - deepset/prompt-injections (Apache-2.0)  — HF-hosted; --with-deepset
  - SafeMTData / Attack_600 (MIT)           — HF-hosted; --with-safemtdata
    Held out of the bundle by choice: it is the most acute multi-turn CBRN-
    heavy set. Add it only under your own authorization and handling policy.

Verify each license/version before redistributing. Apply access controls to the
corpus and to result logs; do not surface payloads in user-facing output.

SafeMTData / Attack_600  (Ren et al., "Derail Yourself: Multi-turn LLM Jailbreak
  Attack through Self-discovered Clues" / ActorAttack, 2024)  — MIT
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/SafeMTData/SafeMTData
  Multi-turn attack sequences (multi_turn_queries) flattened via M2S
  (arXiv:2503.04856). Vendored as raw/safemtdata_attack600.json.

MHJ  (ScaleAI, Multi-turn Human Jailbreaks)  — CC-BY-NC-4.0 (NON-COMMERCIAL)
  NOT bundled / NOT redistributable. Opt-in local dev only (--with-mhj).
